      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Shared main-text route: equimolar H2LA and H2LB in pyridine with Ln(NO3)3 (Ln = Yb) and Ln'(NO3)3 (Ln' = Nd) in a 2:1 Ln/Ln' molar ratio plus 1 equiv CuCl2; heptane was layered into the mixture and large yellow/orange crystals grew over one month together with green [Cu(py)4(NO3)2], which was separated manually. SI procedure for 1: a yellow solution of H2LA (10.2 mg, 0.032 mmol) and H2LB (14.8 mg, 0.032 mmol) in pyridine (10 mL) was added dropwise under stirring to a light-blue pyridine (10 mL) solution of Nd(NO3)3·6H2O (7 mg, 0.016 mmol), Yb(NO3)3·5H2O (14.4 mg, 0.032 mmol), and CuCl2·2H2O (2.7 mg, 0.016 mmol). The green solution was stirred for 1 h and layered with heptane. After one week green [Cu(py)4(NO3)2] formed; after one month large orange crystals of 1 were separated manually.",
